>> title: Roasted Brussels Sprouts
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: brussels sprouts, roast, balsamic, sheet pan, side
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: roasted brussels sprouts, balsamic brussels sprouts, crispy brussels sprouts, roast sprouts, charred brussels
>> pairs-with: polenta, basic-vinaigrette
>> servings: 4
>> time: 40 min
>> step.1: trim and halve, loose leaves kept
>> step.2: toss in oil, salt and pepper
>> step.3: roast 425°F (220°C) 22 min, cut side down
>> step.4: simmer the balsamic to a syrup 4 min
>> step.5: toss off the heat

Trim the dry stem end off @Brussels sprouts{1 1/2%lb}(700 g) and halve each one through the root, keeping every loose leaf that falls off.

Toss @&(~1)halved sprouts{} with @olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @kosher salt{1%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp}, then turn every half cut side up in the bowl so the oil pools on the flat face.

Spread @&(~1)oiled sprouts{} cut side down on a #sheet pan{} heated with the oven and ~roast{22%min} at 425°F (220°C).

Simmer @balsamic vinegar{1/4%cup}(60 mL) with @honey{1%tsp} in a small pan ~simmer{4%min} until it coats the back of a spoon and pulls in a thread off the edge.

Toss @&(~2)roasted sprouts{} with @&(~1)balsamic syrup{} and @flaky salt{1/2%tsp} off the heat.
